// @PLN85 move-on-block-return regression (block-return-move cluster).
//
// An inline block whose tail is a fresh block-LOCAL struct must MOVE (the LHS
// adopts an owned copy), not borrow. Legacy borrowed: `a` and `b` reused the
// same block-local slot, so `a` was clobbered by `b` — this exact minimal shape
// deterministically printed `3 4 3 4` instead of `1 2 3 4`. Kept MINIMAL so the
// slot-reuse corruption manifests deterministically (extra locals perturb the
// layout and mask it). The move fix makes `a` own its store; asserts below fail
// on any regression, and the suite leak gate catches the paired store leak.
struct P { x: integer, y: integer }

fn main() {
  a = {
    z = P { x: 1, y: 2 }; z
  };
  b = {
    z = P { x: 3, y: 4 }; z
  };
  assert(a.x == 1, "a.x moved, not clobbered by b");
  assert(a.y == 2, "a.y moved, not clobbered by b");
  assert(b.x == 3, "b.x");
  assert(b.y == 4, "b.y");
  print("block-return-move ok\n");
}
